<title>USA: AT&amp;T says withdraws bid for US navy contract.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T says withdraws bid for US navy contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>AT&amp;T Corp said it has withdrawn its bid for a $2.934 billion U.S. Navy contract that was awarded to a group of four firms, including AT&amp;T, earlier on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We bid on the whole contract but were allotted only a portion, so under those circumstances, we withdrew the bid,&quot; said Jim Byrnes, a spokesman for AT&amp;T.</p>
<p>The Navy said on Tuesday it awarded the contract for voice, video and data modernization of Navy infrastructure to Lucent Technologies Inc, GTE Government Systems Corp, Bell Atlantic Federal Integrated Systems Inc, and AT&amp;T Government Markets.</p>
<p>The contract is expected to be completed by July 2007.</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8310))</p>
</text>
